<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Supply Chain Innovation Observatory &middot; {{ week }}</title>
<style>
  :root { --ink: #1d2125; --muted: #6b7580; --rule: #e3e6e9; --bg: #ffffff;
          --up: #1f7a4d; --down: #a33a3a; }
  body { margin: 0; background: var(--bg); color: var(--ink);
         font: 15px/1.55 -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; }
  main { max-width: 1080px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 32px 24px 96px; }
  h1 { font-size: 26px; margin: 0 0 4px; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
  h2 { font-size: 17px; margin: 44px 0 12px; padding-bottom: 8px;
       border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  .sub { color: var(--muted); margin: 0 0 24px; font-size: 13px; }
  .health { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; margin: 0 0 8px; padding: 0; list-style: none; }
  .chip { font-size: 12px; padding: 3px 10px; border-radius: 999px; border: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  .chip.ok { background: #edf7f1; border-color: #cfe8db; }
  .chip.stale { background: #fdf6e8; border-color: #f0e0bb; }
  .chip.failed { background: #fbeeee; border-color: #eccccc; }
  table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; font-size: 14px; }
  th, td { text-align: left; padding: 8px 10px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  th { font-weight: 600; color: var(--muted); font-size: 12px;
       text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.04em; }
  td.num { text-align: right; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .up { color: var(--up); } .down { color: var(--down); }
  .empty { color: var(--muted); font-style: italic; }
  footer { margin-top: 56px; color: var(--muted); font-size: 12px;
           border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); padding-top: 16px; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="wrap">
<header>
  <p class="eyebrow">Supply Chain Innovation Observatory &middot; collection health</p>
  <h1>{{ week }}</h1>
</header>

<section>
  <h2>Did the collectors run?</h2>
  <p>This page answers what a week can answer. Everything interpretive &mdash;
  the stage board, substance against attention, lab to field, the build map and
  the evidence behind them &mdash; is in the quarterly report, because a week
  cannot support it: two thirds of technology-weeks hold no observations at all.
  lexicon v{{ lexicon_version }}.</p>
</section>

<div class="panel">
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th class="name">Source</th><th class="tag">Status</th>
      <th class="name">Last run</th><th class="num">Retrieved</th>
      <th class="num">Matched</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      {% for source in sources %}
      <tr>
        <td class="name">{{ source.name }}</td>
        <td class="tag">{{ source.status }}</td>
        <td class="name">{{ source.last_run_week or '&mdash;' }}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ retrieved.get(source.name, 0) }}</td>
        <td class="num">{% set found = arrivals | selectattr('0', 'equalto', source.name) | list %}{{ found[0][1] if found else 0 }}</td>
      </tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

<section>
  <h2>What arrived</h2>
  <p>{{ matched_total }} observations matched this week. A source showing zero
  matched but a retrieved count above it ran and found nothing on the watchlist,
  which is ordinary. A source showing nothing retrieved did not run, and that is
  the thing this page exists to surface.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Rising terms</h2>
  <p class="source">Phrases appearing far more than usual and matching no active technology</p>
  {% if not rising_terms %}
  <p>No new terms rose above the threshold this week.</p>
  {% else %}
  {% if rising_total > rising_terms|length %}
  <p><strong>Showing the {{ rising_terms|length }} strongest of {{ rising_total }}.</strong>
  The rest are in <code>candidate_terms</code>; a capped list that did not say so
  would read as a complete one.</p>
  {% endif %}
  <p>Candidates for the lexicon. The pipeline never edits the watchlist; a human
  merges, through <code>lexicon prepare</code> and <code>lexicon check</code>.</p>
</section>
<div class="panel">
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th class="name">Term</th><th class="num">Count</th>
      <th class="num">Against trailing mean</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      {% for row in rising_terms %}
      <tr><td class="name">{{ row.term }}
        {% if row.examples %}<br>
          {% for title, url in row.examples[:2] %}
            <span class="tag">{% if url and url.startswith('http') %}<a href="{{ url }}">{{ title }}</a>{% else %}{{ title }}{% endif %}</span>
          {% endfor %}
        {% endif %}
      </td><td class="num">{{ row.count }}</td>
      <td class="num">{{ '%.1f'|format(row.ratio) }}&times;</td></tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>
{% endif %}

<footer>
  Collection runs weekly; reporting is quarterly. The quarterly report is
  <code>report-&lt;quarter&gt;.html</code> and its evidence is
  <code>evidence-&lt;quarter&gt;.html</code>.
</footer>
</div>
</body>
</html>
